{% doc %}
  Renders the product media gallery.

  The file was empty. `blocks/_product-media-gallery.liquid` renders it, so the
  product page had no images at all — the one thing a product page cannot do
  without. Everything it needs already existed: `media-gallery.js` documents the
  markup it expects, and `base.css` already styles every class below.

  ## Why a scroll container and not a stack of slides

  The stage is a horizontally scrolling, snapping list. Every image sits at its
  natural position in the document, so lazy loading works, and a customer can
  swipe through the media before any JavaScript has run. The alternative — a
  stack of absolutely positioned slides at `opacity: 0` — downloads every image
  immediately and shows nothing at all until a script sorts it out.

  The stacked layout is the same markup with the scroll axis removed in CSS, so
  the two layouts share one set of nodes rather than branching here.

  ## Filtering images by option

  When enabled, an image belongs to an option value if its alt text ends with
  `|option:value`. Images with no such marker are always shown, because shared
  photography — a size chart, a fabric close-up — belongs to every variant.
  `filter_images_strict` turns that off for stores that have labelled every file.

  Filtering happens here rather than in JavaScript so the first paint is already
  correct; `<variant-picker>` re-filters on change.

  ## Video, models and zoom

  Video and 3D models are wrapped in `<deferred-media>`: the poster is a real
  image and the player lives in a `<template>`, so nothing heavy is fetched
  until someone presses play. Zoom is opt-in per block and only wraps images.

  Parameters:
    product  (product, required)
    section  (object, required)
    settings (object, required)  The block's settings
    block_shopify_attributes (string, optional)

  @example
    {% render 'product-media', product: product, section: section, settings: block.settings %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = settings
  assign layout = s.gallery_layout | default: 'carousel'
  assign ratio = s.gallery_image_ratio | default: 'adapt'
  assign thumbs_position = s.thumbnails_position | default: 'thumbnails-below'
  assign pagination = s.pagination_type | default: 'thumbnails'

  # `navigation` offers none | arrows | chevrons; the last two differ only by
  # glyph, so the value maps straight onto an icon name.
  assign nav_style = s.navigation | default: 'arrows'
  case nav_style
    when 'chevrons'
      assign nav_icon = 'chevron'
    else
      assign nav_icon = 'arrow'
  endcase
  assign current = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign media_items = product.media

  comment
    Variant media filtering. `hide_variants` keeps only the media attached to the
    selected variant plus anything not attached to any variant, which is the
    behaviour merchants mean by "hide unselected variant media".
  endcomment
  if s.hide_variants and current.featured_media != blank
    assign kept = ''
    for item in product.media
      assign is_variant_media = false
      for variant in product.variants
        if variant.featured_media.id == item.id
          assign is_variant_media = true
          break
        endif
      endfor

      if is_variant_media == false or item.id == current.featured_media.id
        assign kept = kept | append: item.id | append: ','
      endif
    endfor
    assign kept_ids = kept | split: ','
  endif

  comment
    Option filtering reads `SEO text|option:value` from the alt text. The value
    is compared without case, because a merchant typing "Mango" into Files and
    "mango" into the option is describing the same thing.
  endcomment
  if s.enable_filter_images
    assign selected_values = ''
    for option in product.options_with_values
      assign selected_values = selected_values | append: option.selected_value | downcase | append: ','
    endfor
  endif

  assign gap = s.gallery_gap | default: 10
-%}

<media-gallery
  id="gallery-{{ section.id }}"
  class="product-media product-media--{{ layout }} product-media--{{ thumbs_position }}"
  data-layout="{{ layout }}"
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  {% if s.enable_gallery_loop %}data-loop="true"{% endif %}
  {% if s.sticky_gallery %}data-sticky="true"{% endif %}
  style="--gallery-gap: {{ gap }}px;"
  {% render 'spacing', block: s %}
  {{ block_shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The stage is focusable and labelled as a group so a keyboard user reaches the
    media and hears what it is before the arrow keys mean anything.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="product-media__stage"
    data-ref="stage"
    tabindex="0"
    role="group"
    aria-label="{{ 'products.product.gallery' | t: product: product.title | escape }}"
  >
    {%- for item in media_items -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign show = true

        if s.hide_variants and current.featured_media != blank
          assign show = false
          for id in kept_ids
            if id == item.id
              assign show = true
              break
            endif
          endfor
        endif

        if show and s.enable_filter_images
          assign alt_raw = item.alt | default: ''
          if alt_raw contains '|option:'
            assign marker = alt_raw | split: '|option:' | last | downcase | strip
            assign show = false
            for value in selected_values
              if value == marker
                assign show = true
                break
              endif
            endfor
          elsif s.filter_images_strict
            assign show = false
          endif
        endif

        assign clean_alt = item.alt | default: product.title | split: '|' | first
      -%}

      {%- if show -%}
        <div
          class="product-media__item{% if forloop.first and s.gallery_full_width_first %} product-media__item--wide{% endif %}"
          data-media
          data-media-id="{{ item.id }}"
          data-media-type="{{ item.media_type }}"
        >
          {%- case item.media_type -%}
            {%- when 'image' -%}
              {%- if s.enable_image_zoom -%}
                <media-zoom
                  class="product-media__zoom"
                  data-zoom-src="{{ item | image_url: width: 2048 }}"
                  data-level="2"
                >
                  {% render 'image',
                     image: item,
                     alt: clean_alt,
                     ratio: ratio,
                     class: 'product-media__image',
                     id: 'zoom-image',
                     priority: forloop.first,
                     sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 50vw, 100vw' %}

                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="product-media__zoom-trigger"
                    data-ref="trigger"
                    aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.open_zoom' | t }}"
                  >
                    {% render 'icon', icon: 'zoom-in', size: 18 %}
                  </button>
                </media-zoom>
              {%- else -%}
                {% render 'image',
                   image: item,
                   alt: clean_alt,
                   ratio: ratio,
                   class: 'product-media__image',
                   priority: forloop.first,
                   sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 50vw, 100vw' %}
              {%- endif -%}

            {%- when 'video' or 'external_video' -%}
              <deferred-media class="product-media__video" data-autoplay="false">
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="product-media__play"
                  data-ref="poster"
                  aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.play_video' | t }}"
                >
                  {% render 'image',
                     image: item.preview_image,
                     alt: clean_alt,
                     ratio: ratio,
                     class: 'product-media__poster',
                     sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 50vw, 100vw' %}
                  {% render 'icon', icon: 'play', size: 28 %}
                </button>

                <template data-ref="template">
                  {%- if item.media_type == 'video' -%}
                    {{ item | video_tag: controls: true, playsinline: true, preload: 'none' }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{ item | external_video_tag: loading: 'lazy' }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </template>
              </deferred-media>

            {%- when 'model' -%}
              <deferred-media class="product-media__model" data-autoplay="false">
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="product-media__play"
                  data-ref="poster"
                  aria-label="{{ 'products.product.view_in_space' | t }}"
                >
                  {% render 'image',
                     image: item.preview_image,
                     alt: clean_alt,
                     ratio: ratio,
                     class: 'product-media__poster',
                     sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 50vw, 100vw' %}
                  {% render 'icon', icon: 'grid', size: 28 %}
                </button>

                <template data-ref="template">
                  {{ item | model_viewer_tag: reveal: 'interaction', toggleable: true }}
                </template>
              </deferred-media>

            {%- else -%}
              {{ item }}
          {%- endcase -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A product with no media still needs a box of the right shape, or the two
        columns collapse and the buy button jumps up the page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="product-media__item product-media__item--empty" data-media data-media-id="0" data-media-type="image">
        {{ 'product-apparel-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'product-media__image placeholder-svg' }}
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>

  {%- if pagination == 'thumbnails' and product.media.size > 1 -%}
    <media-thumbnails
      class="product-media__thumbnails"
      data-ref="thumbnails"
      data-size="{{ s.thumbnail_size | default: 'medium' }}"
      data-style="{{ s.thumbnail_style | default: 'round' }}"
    >
      {%- for item in media_items -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="product-media__thumbnail"
          data-thumbnail
          data-media-id="{{ item.id }}"
          aria-current="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
          aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.go_to_slide' | t: index: forloop.index }}"
        >
          {% render 'image',
             image: item.preview_image,
             alt: '',
             ratio: 'square',
             sizes: '120px',
             widths: '120,240' %}

          {%- unless item.media_type == 'image' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              A video thumbnail that looks like a photograph is a photograph as
              far as the customer is concerned, so the type is marked.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="product-media__thumbnail-badge" aria-hidden="true">
              {% render 'icon', icon: 'play', size: 12 %}
            </span>
          {%- endunless -%}
        </button>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </media-thumbnails>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    ---------- Navigation and position ----------
    `navigation` and two of the three `pagination_type` values had no markup at
    all: only thumbnails were ever rendered, so a merchant choosing "arrows" or
    "fraction" changed nothing on the page.

    Both now render the shared control components, so the gallery inherits the
    icon, size, colour and gradient settings the collection carousels use and
    the two cannot drift apart. `media-gallery.js` drives them through
    `@theme/carousel-controls`; no Swiper is involved.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
    {%- if pagination == 'controls' -%}
      {% render 'carousel-controls', settings: s, align: 'center' %}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- if nav_style != 'none' -%}
        {% render 'carousel-nav',
           settings: s,
           icon: nav_icon,
           position: 'inside' %}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The gallery writes the current position here. Without it a screen reader user
    swiping through media hears nothing change.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="visually-hidden" data-ref="status" role="status"></p>
</media-gallery>
